mantle rm318
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_berit_coalworth
title the returning chime
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=priest
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk traces_echoes_of_the_chapel_bell_across_a_map
likes hard_cheese old_tales old_maps warm_rain
dislikes drizzle deep_mud
fears a_muddy_church_sill a_tower_out_of_hearing
hopes a_high_room_with_an_echo a_map_of_every_listening_place
topics lore +0.6 travel +0.5 pastimes +0.4 weather +0.3 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=discreet refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# traces the return journey of a bell stroke on a map, can make an old tale last the length of a shower and seeks a high room where the chapel may still be heard.

words
oath! = Crack the clapper  |  Rattle my hinge
saying! = The returning note belongs to every ear  |  Listen past the first stroke
map = a soft old map | my folded hill sheet
ring = the returning note | a thin bronze aftersound
mark = a crescent of chalk | my curved chalk mark
morsel = a fine slice of hard cheese | the pale cheese shaving
tying = a bell-rope knot | the little binding hitch
post = the dark doorpost | the long upright
hearth = a sun-warmed ledge | a patch of warm stone
oldpage = the faded lane | a street in pale ink
grain = the narrow crack | a finger of worn stone
rag = my dry knee cloth | a folded scrap of sacking
rind = the last cheese rind | a tough yellow edge
wetsoft = a mean spit of rain | that floating damp
mud = a boot-deep hollow | the clay by the lower step
seal = a small pin mark | a map pinprick
dayend = the late bronze stroke | an evening peal
ledger = my pocket notebook | the little black book
tower = the nearest tower | a high bell opening

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : A door left quiet for a grieving wolf and swept for a muddy one is one part of worship I can do well.
opinion @2 road for 1 : A walk through a folded map always discloses something the ink couldn't make out.
opinion @3 strangers for 1 : A new ear stands in a doorway and hears a note the regulars have stopped noticing.
opinion @4 city for 2 : There are corners of Ridgemere where a chapel across town may as well be whispering at your shoulder.
opinion @5 houses mixed 0 : I admire a soundly roofed hall. I also think the good dry space under it ought to welcome more feet.
opinion @6 sump against 1 : Childhood mud catches at the heel a long time after the climbing begins. I'd keep my last shoes on higher boards.
opinion @7 dole for 2 : A piece of bread ought to go straight to the waiting mouth. Reverence needn't slow the hand.
opinion @8 festivals for 1 : All those bells lend the city a different set of streets to find its way along.
opinion @9 times against 1 : When a bit of hard cheese must go three ways, the ringing grows louder at an empty table.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Your footfall's welcome inside this patch of quiet. | Come where it's easy to hear a low voice.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Welcome as the day begins its ringing. | Morning. A fine hour for listening from a doorway.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Leave the mud its due at the sill. Come in. | Welcome out of that spray about your ears.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : Stand by me where you can watch my hands. | A welcome from the working side of the threshold.
line @5 greet.return : Your greeting came back warm from the wall. | I heard you clearly and I'm glad.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Familiar feet have their own little peal. | Welcome into the comfortable hearing distance.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=night] : Good company late on a quiet round. | A voice beside the last note of the evening.
line @8 farewell : Keep an ear out for the turn that leads home. | May the bright side of the hill be yours.
line @9 farewell.return : I'll listen to the steps go safely out. | Carry what you need of this quiet with you.
line @10 again.open : A second passing like a returning chime. | Our road has doubled round its fold again.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kindred can ask their questions from the close side. | Pull the family seat round toward my good ear.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here in the bell's shadow! | Look where the high note comes back!
line @13 react.news : Set the report down where we can hear what follows it. | I shall listen for the quiet part of the account.
line @14 react.news.new : That note has reached me for the first time. | A fresh road opening on the page.
line @15 react.news.known : I've heard the first telling ring through already. | That account has its mark beside an earlier hearing.
line @16 react.news.doubt : I'm hearing more of the echo than the first account. | I'd like to find the place the first clear word came from.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : A sad stroke needs a shoulder beside it. | Let's sit through the silence that follows such a word.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : Let that sound carry to the furthest sill. | I'd set a bell swinging for news so welcome.
line @19 answer.how : Keeping pace with my own restless feet. | Fit for another climb if the view's worth it.
line @20 decline : I'd lose the other end of my work if I took that on. | That would leave a promise hanging with nobody to mind it.
line @21 accept_decline : Your reasons have had a fair hearing. | A kindly limit is still a kindness.
line @22 sympathise : Sit here. I can carry the next little duty across for you. | I'll give that ache some quiet company while you rest.
line @23 thank : A kindness with a long sweet echo. | You've smoothed some broken paving under my feet.
line @24 deflect_thanks : I was crossing the room that way in any case. | Let the kind word go out to somebody further off.
line @25 preclose : I've another listening place to mark before I forget. | Time to see where my own footsteps lead next.
line @26 accept_preclose : Go where your next clear stroke is calling. | I shall hear the ending long enough.
line @27 farewell [here.weather=rain] : Keep the folded edge against your coat. | May the mud release your boots without argument.
line @28 farewell.return [here.time=night] : A warm sill when the night round ends. | Rest within hearing of a kindly voice.
line @29 greet [pair.band=friends] : Here comes a welcome sort of echo. | The map had room for a friend at this turning.
line @30 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Enough purpose for my hands and motion for my feet. | Still sweeping in time with the stroke.
line @31 preclose [here.time=dusk] : I should make a mark before there's too little light for chalk. | Time for the evening edge of my round.

scene mapring
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mark# on #map# means the bell stroke came back instead of dying there. | Every crescent on my sheet is a place with two bells for the price of one.
b : Which was the first sound? | A second tower just out of sight?
a : The tower's stroke. The other belongs to a stone face along the lane. | One bell and a good wall will make a proper little duet.

scene cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shave #morsel# thin enough to take light at the edge. | Hard cheese belongs in my pocket when there's walking to do.
b : Does the taste change when it's thin? | What keeps it from oiling the map?
a : Quite. The salt spreads up the edge before the rest has warmed. | Two separate folds. I don't care to navigate by grease marks.

scene oldturn
when topic=lore self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long tale needs a pause a wolf can stand in. | Old tales tell you which turning to listen at if you learn them by heart.
b : Where do you put yours? | What do you hear there?
a : Where the walker might go wrong. Give every ear a chance to choose. | The first little doubt that the easy road's the proper one.

scene drizz
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #wetsoft# eats a chalk mark without ever washing the wall clean. | Drizzle wants to settle in every crease of my map.
b : Would a pin hole last longer? | Why keep opening it in the rain?
a : #seal# for position, chalk for the sound. Different witnesses. | Because I lose the precise turn once I'm two doors further on.

scene warm
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm rain finds the higher notes in the paving. | I like looking up when the rain feels warmer than a dry sleeve.
b : How can stone make a high note? | Your paper might feel otherwise about it.
a : Strike shallow stone in small drops and there's music enough. | I wrap the map and give my face the whole shower.

scene bootpull
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : How would you free a heel from #mud# without leaving the shoe? | What is the least undignified way to get out of deep clay?
b : Give the foot a slow twist before you lift. | Find a solid shoulder and use it. The mud feels no embarrassment.
a : Yes. Better than tugging straight up like an impatient bell ringer. | Fair words. I'll offer my shoulder first if somebody goes in ahead.

scene sexton
when topic=work self.job=priest self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I earn the quiet by sweeping the entry before the first steps come. | I find #post# at #self.workplace# by touch and listen before I open.
b : Why does sweeping earn quiet? | Which sound do you expect outside?
a : Feet can settle softly when there isn't grit giving every footfall away. | A step waiting outside. I'd hate to fling a door against an early guest.

scene learning
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first lesson is what a room sounds like before you start doing things to it. | Each learner takes a quiet moment before the work changes hands.
b : That sounds very little like a lesson. | What happens in the interval?
a : Few wolves ever try it on their own. Then a creak can tell you something. | You hear who's already at work beyond the door.

scene higher
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I was brought up where mud gets the last word. I'd fancy a room with better acoustics. | I want to end my climbing with still a little of the hill below my window.
b : Whose words would you hear up there? | And can you still hear your bell?
a : A chapel voice or a passing wolf. Anything better than mud pulling at soles. | That's why I mark my map instead of choosing by the height alone.

scene friendview
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll find a listening place wide enough for #self.friend# and me. | I'd lend #self.friend# my best marked map for a quiet evening.
b : What if your friend can't catch that second note? | Wouldn't you miss your own marks?
a : Then I'd be interested to learn what another ear did catch. | I can verify the marks by walking those hills. I'd like the excuse.

scene estate
when topic=land self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Estate walls throw back a different sort of footfall from plain street walls. | By the Estate walks a tree can interrupt the finest echo halfway home.
b : Does the step sound more dignified? | How does a tree get between a bell and a wall?
a : Only if it's walking with dignity in the first place. Stone reflects what's there. | Gathers the sound among the leaves. Try again when winter has stripped it.

scene oldplace
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A black line drawn up the hill above Ridgemere can't tell you how the slope feels. | Turn the map east and a wet stair still goes stubbornly uphill.
b : Can a mark tell you anything one's legs can't? | So why turn it at all?
a : Where a bell will reach your ear while you're resting those legs. | I enjoy seeing the city's outline from the direction I'm bound for.

scene rind
when topic=food
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take #rind# with you for broth. It has one more job in it. | Try the thin shaving. I'll keep the tough rim for my pot.
b : I'd welcome a thick taste in thin soup. | You'll want some of the good bit yourself.
a : Scrape the dry side first. There's a comfortable mouthful waiting in it. | I've kept a fair piece. My generosity likes a sound footing.

scene uncertainty
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A word at a distance can sound like five different mouths in agreement. | Give a rumour a fine stone wall and it comes back sounding authoritative.
b : Wouldn't all the voices have different notes? | Then would you hush the wall?
a : If they were really five. Listen for an identical little break in the middle. | I'd find the mouth before I gave the wall a reply.

scene poorpot
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take the warmed place while I see if the pot has another share. | There's a little space by #hearth# if supper's going to be late.
b : Warm seating with a small crust would answer. | I'll stay till the warmth comes through my coat.
a : Then let's begin by settling you warm and look for the bread together. | I'll sit your other side. The stone's generous for a little while.

scene roadplan
when topic=travel
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Next walk I mean to cross the exact point where a chapel drops out of hearing. | I want to find the lane with no stroke at all on my return map.
b : How do you know you've crossed it? | What if the whole city hears every bell?
a : Back three paces at the next peal. The line is somewhere under my heel. | Then I've a nice day's walking before I get to prove it.

scene deacon
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't ask a learner to mend a hinge with a hymn. | A good keyed joint knows the difference between pressure and a prayer.
b : Wouldn't a hymn make the work a little lighter? | Are you teaching reverence or woodwork?
a : Certainly. But fetch the oil first and leave your other paw free. | Care. Quite a lot of care wears either set of clothes.

scene priestchair
when topic=work self.job=priest
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want to place a chair where a quiet visitor can sit without being expected at the front. | I measure a swept space by what a tired guest can do with it.
b : Near the door for a quick escape? | What else belongs beside the chair?
a : Near enough. Rest isn't an agreement to join a procession. | Room to turn a sore knee without a whole bench getting up.

scene oldink
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #oldpage# on a map of mine ends in a curious little hook. | The page suggests a road that turns sharply toward a blank square.
b : Did somebody mean to draw a chapel there? | Has the road actually finished?
a : Or a tree, or a well. I enjoy going to look before I make up my story. | The end of the ink. The road may have quite a bit to say beyond.

scene clayprice
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Good boots are an expensive way of measuring the mud a whole street can hold. | I'd pay more for one sound step than for a week of promises to mend it.
b : Somebody must promise the work before it starts. | A stone step's dear in its own right.
a : Fair. I'd have the promise followed by a properly chosen stone. | So I'd put it where every passing sole can get some use from it.

scene feast
when topic=season
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A feast peal can bring a whole respectable street out to its windows. | I enjoy watching a crowd listen before it gets busy speaking.
b : Who would you be watching first? | Is there much chance of that at a festival?
a : The last wolf at the furthest window. Makes a fine end to a line. | One breath between the beginning of a peal and the first shout of recognition.

scene chapelroof
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'm uneasy at water striking the same patch over and over by a sill. | The rain's been working its way toward my folded chart.
b : A little can be wiped up before anybody slips. | I can hold the dry corner up for you.
a : I'll see to it with #rag#. No use asking a foot to discover the trouble. | Kind. Hold it till the crease has a proper roof.

scene quietrest
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Can you picture a bed where the late peal comes straight through a high shutter? | My ideal room has two listening places and only one chair.
b : What would keep the rain out of that room? | Where does the second listener sit?
a : A slant in the slats. Sound has a kinder notion of visiting than water. | The corner that holds a standing wolf and a fine echo. I'll lend the chair.

scene paperwork
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enter #dayend# in #ledger# by the length of its tail. | I mark a faint bell return with one curve and a strong one with two.
b : How do you measure the tail of a sound? | Which one gets the name attached?
a : Count the breaths before ordinary street talk comes clear around it. | The faint one more often. A strong tower's easy enough to find again.

scene showroute
when topic=newcomer
does offer / accept / assess
a : Here, take my drawn turn if you're seeking the middle streets. | I can walk as far as the second chime with you if you like.
b : I'd sooner have the voice of a guide at the first corner. | Two chimes would be plenty. What's the road beyond like?
a : Then I'll come until the chalk and the paving have properly met. | Firm if you avoid the dark hollow under the broken spout.

scene winterdoor
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cold hinge can make a remarkable imitation of a much smaller bell. | I check a draught beside #post# with the lightest shaving in my pocket.
b : How do you silence the hinge? | Does the shaving need to be wood?
a : Oil, time and a gentle swing. It deserves to have an easy winter too. | Cheese works in a pinch, though it's a poor use of a good supper.

scene handnote
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a shape you can draw for a note without knowing the least of music. | I use a hook of chalk for something the ear loses at the end.
b : Would a singer recognise it? | Which shape would represent an endless sound?
a : A walker who listens might. I'm not writing for a choir yet. | I wouldn't try. Bell rope wears; even the finest note takes its leave.

scene bothcall
when topic=lore
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I like the tale where the bell answers the lost traveller twice. | A good old story can guide a wolf a little way in the dark.
b : Some folk might say it just echoed. | The road in a story doesn't have real holes in it.
a : Of course it echoed. The traveller still heard an answer and found the way. | Quite. Look at the real road with your other eye while you're listening.

scene clearview
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wagon late on a wet afternoon can keep a whole entry full of waiting feet. | A delayed wagon gives me time to see which waiting wolf has nowhere dry to sit.
b : Are you going to give the crowd a song? | You'd miss the wheels coming yourself.
a : A few chairs will do more good at first. Voices will find each other. | If I'm making somebody more comfortable I can bear to be second at the door.

scene laststairs
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I want to mount a final house stair and hear the low voices clearly from below. | One well-chosen upper sill would let me retain the finest thing about my beginnings.
b : Some wolves want to leave every low sound behind. | Which part of the lower streets would you keep?
a : That's too much leaving. I only want a bed out of the mud. | Feet coming home near enough together to see each other safe.

story echo_penny [topic=lore]
  : There's an old story of a traveller trying to pay the second chapel after hearing its bell answer the first. Couldn't find the second door.
  : An elderly wolf pointed to a smooth wall. The traveller tapped a copper against it and the sound came back.
  b : Was the debt reckoned paid?
  : The traveller left the copper at the only chapel door and gave the wall a very cordial farewell.

story map_rip [topic=pastimes]
  : A map tore along the exact line where I thought the road ought to bend. I tied the halves with a slack loop of thread.
  : Out walking, the string blew over the paper and pointed up an entirely different hill.
  b : Which way did you go?
  : Up the hill. My road was still marked and the weather didn't often give such explicit directions.

story cheesepeal [topic=food]
  : I shaved a hard cheese rind by a very resonant wall. Each scrape made a little chirrup behind me.
  : I tried a different angle and got two chirrups every stroke.
  b : Did you find out what answered?
  : A loose pane in a wooden shutter. I ate the cheese and left the fitting a good snug wedge in payment for the music.

story quiet_step [topic=work]
  : I swept a doorstep clean enough to hear the difference when a single small stone rolled onto it. I meant to fetch the broom at once.
  : Then a sparrow hopped down and nudged the stone three times with its bill.
  b : Did you leave the bird to finish sweeping?
  : Until the little seed came into view. A perfect floor can be an inconvenient thing for a hungry visitor.

story upper_bowl [topic=dreams]
  : I once carried supper up a whole hill to see whether the land looked any different with no hunger pulling at me. Sat down on a high stone.
  : A bell reached me as I was lifting the bowl. It set a ripple going on my spoon.
  b : Could a bell do that all the way up a hill?
  : No. It was my own excited paw. The sound had arrived just the same.

rule @echo
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two clear returns off that wall. | There's a new little hook for my map.

rule @doors
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=priest
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hear the waiting step before you open. | That sweep leaves the chair a clean way in.

rule @lesson
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First discover the room's ordinary noise. | May I see how you set the tool down?

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Scant use putting chalk under that runnel. | The centre fold wants cover first.

rule @cheese
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hard enough to shave clear across. | Save the rind for another mouthful.

rule @road
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The ink arrives before the walking does. | A rectangle of paper can't show that climb.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : There's a comfortable listening place here. You're welcome to it.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a good returning sound in my day.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The evening makes a small voice audible over a long way.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Let's stand a pace apart and see whether one civil word can travel between us.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=priest self.workplace] : I see to the practical needs of #self.workplace#, down to the stone under your boot.
dlg @6 resident.job : I finish the unattended small duties before the largest crowd comes through.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Carry the kindly sound as far as it will travel.
dlg @8 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : You can begin by listening to the work before you put a hand on it.
dlg @9 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : Teaching must wait for another occasion. One small question may fit between duties.
dlg @10 master.work : Steady handling, a sense of which thing comes first, and some attention to the wolf who comes after.
dlg @11 master.wages : Learning brings no wages. You may sell your finished work. Learning goes faster at my elbow.
dlg @12 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : #here.take_on_why# I like the grounds for a decision heard clearly.
dlg @13 master.refused : #topic.why# There is the part we must attend to.
dlg @14 master.bye : Leave your hands easy. A good lesson carries past the hour.
dlg @15 church.greet [here.day=rest] : A welcome within these walls. The Restday service is #here.service#.
dlg @16 church.greet [here.day!=rest] : Come in while the floor's quiet and find yourself a place.
dlg @17 church.service [here.day=rest] : Today you can join us for #here.service#. There's a place open within hearing.
dlg @18 church.service [here.day!=rest] : On Restday we have #here.service#. You're welcome to come and listen.
dlg @19 church.poor : Restday bread reaches the households most in need. Come and ask about a share.
dlg @20 church.offering : Anything freely spared can help us make another welcome.
dlg @21 church.thanked : Your gift adds another place where someone can sit and eat.
dlg @22 church.refused : #topic.why# The willing thought is welcome here.
dlg @23 church.bye : May the Bright One light the part of your road I can't see.

graft resident.hub
choice What does the curved mark mean? -> echo_mark
node echo_mark
say A bell struck out of sight, a wall returning it to my ear. Come when the stroke is sounded and hear the sound come home.
choice Are you mapping a way home too? -> echo_room
choice Let's fold the chart for now. -> hub
node echo_room
say Yes. I want a room high on the hill and I'm finding where the lower city's sounds can still reach. A dry room doesn't have to be a deaf one.
choice A good use for a map. -> hub
choice May you find that room. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice Why listen before beginning? -> work_ear
node work_ear
say Any wooden joint will tell you when it has begun to carry extra weight. Listen to the empty room first and you know which creak is the new one.
choice Then do you oil the joint? -> first_look
choice Tell me about the lesson. -> learn
node first_look
say Look where the pressure came from first. There's no use quieting a good warning until you see what it warns against.
choice I'd hear what the work involves. -> work
choice I'll begin by listening. -> bye
